cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  A support-cell secretome program in human hippocampal aging is
  directionally reproducible but not gene-specific
message: >-
  This repository is the home of the manuscript of that title and of the analysis
  code and result tables behind it. Both are in one Zenodo record; cite the DOI
  below. The CFF format has no publication type, so this file declares the
  repository as software.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shimozaki
    given-names: Koji
    affiliation: >-
      Brain Science Research Unit, Graduate School of Biomedical Sciences,
      Nagasaki University, Nagasaki 852-8523, Japan
    email: shimozak@nagasaki-u.ac.jp
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22640702
repository-code: https://github.com/kojishimozaki/human-hippocampal-aging-secretome
version: v2.1
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22640702
    description: >-
      Concept DOI. Always resolves to the newest version of the deposit, which is
      what the manuscript cites.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22640703
    description: >-
      First version. Code and result tables only; the manuscript PDF and its
      figures were added in the version after it.
keywords:
  - hippocampal aging
  - single-nucleus multiome
  - secretome
  - reanalysis of public data
  - matched-null controls
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  Pre-specified reanalysis of public human hippocampal single-nucleus multiome
  data (GSE268609, with GSE278576, GSE299139, GSE186538, GSE199243, GSE264692
  and GSE325391) through a 2,224-gene secretome lens, with donor-level
  statistics, donor-label permutation calibration of the design itself, and
  expression- and effect-matched null controls for every reported claim.
  Includes the pre-specified analysis documents, the result tables underlying
  every number in the manuscript, and pinned software environments.
